  "body": "[According to the spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/C/#hidden-state-(type=hidden):attr-fe-name-charset), the check for the `_charset_` string in `<input type=hidden name=\"_charset_\">` should be case sensitive, [but in chrome and safari, the check is case insensitive](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=hidden-charset-case-sensitive).\r\n\r\nI was going to make the check case sensitive in chrome to match the spec, but I did an HTTPArchive query and found that there are a few sites which use `_CHARSET_` instead of `_charset_`. Considering that I might be breaking some websites by making the check case sensitive, could we instead change the spec to make the check case insensitive?",
